# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file for the "Cite this repository"
# button and Zenodo reads it when archiving a release.
#
# `version` and `date-released` are left out on purpose: semantic-release bumps
# pyproject.toml only, so a hand-written version here would go stale after the
# next release. Zenodo takes the version from the release tag.
#
# Once Zenodo has minted the concept DOI, add:
#   doi: 10.5281/zenodo.<concept-id>
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pysie2d in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "pysie2d: a 2-D surface-integral-equation solver for electromagnetic scattering"
abstract: >-
  A 2-D surface-integral-equation solver for time-harmonic electromagnetic
  scattering from smooth cylinders (circular or Gielis-superformula
  cross-section) in a homogeneous, half-space or layered background, with
  quasi-normal-mode extraction and finite clusters. Validated against
  analytic Mie theory, a two-cylinder addition-theorem solution, MEEP and
  dolfinx.
authors:
  - given-names: Claudio
    family-names: Silvestre Castro
    email: claudio.silvestre.castro@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/claudio-sc/pysie2d"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/pysie2d/"
keywords:
  - boundary integral equations
  - computational electromagnetics
  - Mie scattering
  - quasi-normal modes
  - nanophotonics
